		{
			"id": "MVB-001",
			"title": "Action picker silently drops failed initial data delivery",
			"severity": "medium",
			"confidence": "high",
			"guarantees": ["G2"],
			"reproduction": "Run ci-bin/lua probes/receipts.lua SOURCE_ROOT. Open the production ui.action_picker through its public API, retain the actual pool route, make the native evaluateJavaScript boundary throw, and deliver a correctly named ready message from the exact attached view. The exception is swallowed, no ERROR is recorded, and the view remains open. Repeat with hs.json.encode throwing: zero native delivery attempts, zero errors, view remains open. Healthy delivery and exact-source confirmation controls pass. This is a Linux Lua boundary replay, not a native Darwin/WebKit execution.",
			"root_cause": "ui/action_picker/init.lua push_init protects encoding and evaluateJavaScript with pcall but ignores the failure values and never reports a failure. It also provides no completion observer. Its ready and didFinishNavigation entries both use this same unchecked delivery.",
			"silent_failure": "The inner pcall consumes the raised boundary exception before ControllerPool.dispatch can log it. Logger.info still says that the picker opened. The custom probe observes zero central error messages; native stderr and asynchronous WebKit default error logging were not measured.",
			"regression_test": "Drive the production picker and pool with correct native name/source and force encoding exception and evaluation exception independently. Require a fixed-metadata ERROR or explicit failed/opening state, with private action data withheld; preserve healthy init, confirmation, foreign-source rejection and stale-session controls. Add completion handling qualified against adapters.webview_result nil and {code=0} success sentinels.",
			"command": "/workspace/scratch/parity-toolchain/ci-bin/lua /workspace/scratch/parity-native-ui/macos-webview/probes/receipts.lua /workspace/worktrees/parity-2026-11-05/macos-webview",
			"evidence_log": "/workspace/scratch/parity-native-ui/macos-webview/logs/receipts.log",
			"root_cause_location": "static/ergopti_plus/macos/ui/action_picker/init.lua:246-261",
			"source_report": "docs/audits/platform-parity/2026-11-05-native-ui/macos-webview/report.md",
			"basis": {
				"kind": "actual production Lua owners over explicit native-port fixtures, plus stated Linux native controls",
				"native_limits": "Linux host only. Windows AHK/WebView2 and Darwin Hammerspoon/WebKit/launchd/System Extensions receiving boundaries were not executed. See scope report for exact synthetic input and source-only joins."
			},
