		{
			"id": "MVB-002",
			"title": "Shortcut auto-close destroys the unsaved draft after a refused hotstring save",
			"severity": "medium",
			"confidence": "high",
			"guarantees": [],
			"reproduction": "Enable close-on-add and open the personal hotstring editor through its registered native shortcut. The actual host initData carries open_mode=shortcut and auto_close=true. Add a unique trigger/output and click Save. The actual shared page sends save then independent close. Make an external private-file writer win at the native CAS publication boundary (or refuse the native write). The real macOS editor and real shared writer refuse publication, log two errors and issue one notification; the following close message still invokes delete. Reopen and deliver ready: the real host initData has no attempted draft. Replay probes/autoclose-host.lua SOURCE_ROOT NODE_CLI ARTIFACT_ROOT; it runs the complete production JS script and actual public macOS editor/parser/writer with only native ports modeled.",
			"root_cause": "_shared/ui/hotstring_editor/script.js saveEntry(false) calls persist() then posts close whenever shortcut mode and autoClose are true, without a save acknowledgement. ui/hotstring_editor/init.lua handles save failure locally but retains no candidate or close veto, and its independent close action unconditionally calls M.close(). The draft exists only in the retiring page; a new page is initialized from disk.",
			"silent_failure": "The refused publication is loud: central error logging and an error notification occur. They contain no attempted trigger/output and are not recovery storage. The subsequent automatic deletion and missing draft on reopen have no preservation or retry protocol. This finding is loss of the refused draft, not the optimistic Saved toast or absence of a diagnostic.",
			"regression_test": "Drive the complete production JS saveEntry/persist/toLua with actual host-provided shortcut/auto_close values and route its generated messages into the real macOS public editor and real TOML writer. Refuse a real-file CAS and native write separately; require the draft to remain open/recoverable until an exact successful save acknowledgement or explicit user discard. Preserve healthy save+close/reopen persistence and refusal controls with auto-close disabled or menu mode. A loud error alone must not satisfy the preservation assertion.",
			"command": "/workspace/scratch/parity-toolchain/ci-bin/lua /workspace/scratch/parity-native-ui/macos-webview/probes/autoclose-host.lua /workspace/worktrees/parity-2026-11-05/macos-webview /workspace/scratch/parity-toolchain/ci-bin/node /workspace/scratch/parity-native-ui/macos-webview",
			"evidence_log": "/workspace/scratch/parity-native-ui/macos-webview/logs/autoclose.log",
			"root_cause_location": "static/ergopti_plus/_shared/ui/hotstring_editor/script.js:1280-1293; static/ergopti_plus/macos/ui/hotstring_editor/init.lua:425-515",
			"additional_property": "Preserve unsaved draft after a refused publication, including automatic close.",
